Statements:
[
    "高血压患者应重点关注饮食事项。",
    "核心 principle is 'low salt, high potassium, fat control, balanced diet'.",
    "Strict salt restriction is the most critical measure.",
    "Daily sodium salt intake should be ≤ 5 grams (about one beer bottle cap).",
    "Avoid high-salt seasonings: soy sauce, broad bean paste, monosodium glutamate, chicken essence, oyster sauce, fermented tofu, pickles, preserved vegetables, cured meat, sausages, ham, and other cured products.",
    "Be cautious of 'hidden salt': bread, dried noodles, biscuits, potato chips, dried plums, canned food, instant soup mixes, and takeout meals.",
    "Use natural spices instead of salt: vinegar, lemon juice, ginger, garlic, scallions, cilantro, star anise, cassia bark, and herbs.",
    "Increase potassium-rich foods to counteract sodium's blood pressure-raising effect.",
    "Target potassium intake is 3500–5000 mg daily for those with normal kidney function.",
    "Recommended potassium-rich fruits: bananas, oranges, tangerines, honeydew melon, avocados.",
    "Recommended potassium-rich vegetables: spinach, broccoli, potatoes (with skin), tomatoes, mushrooms, nori.",
    "Recommended potassium-rich legumes and nuts: red beans, mung beans, soybeans, lentils, almonds, peanuts (unsalted, plain).",
    "Patients with chronic kidney disease (especially eGFR < 60 mL/min/1.73m²) or hyperkalemia must restrict potassium under medical guidance and must not supplement potassium blindly.",
    "Scientifically control fat intake.",
    "Reduce or avoid saturated fats: fatty meat, animal offal, lard, cream, butter, coconut oil, palm oil.",
    "Reduce or avoid trans fats: margarine, shortening, fried foods (fried chicken, french fries), commercially baked goods, milk tea, non-dairy creamer.",
    "Recommend healthy fats: plant oils such as olive oil, camellia oil, flaxseed oil, rapeseed oil (cooking oil total limited to 25–30 grams per day).",
    "Recommend omega-3 rich deep-sea fish: salmon, sardines, mackerel, consumed 2–3 times per week.",
    "Practice the DASH diet pattern.",
    "Eat more: fresh vegetables (4–5 servings/day), fruits (4–5 servings/day), whole grains (e.g., oats, brown rice, whole wheat bread), low-fat or fat-free dairy products.",
    "Consume in moderation: fish, skinless poultry, legumes, nuts (plain, unsalted).",
    "Limit: red meat (e.g., pork, beef, lamb), sweets (cakes, candy, ice cream), sugar-sweetened beverages (cola, fruit juice, milk tea, sports drinks).",
    "Avoid sugar-sweetened beverages (they directly raise blood pressure and promote obesity and insulin resistance).",
    "Limit alcohol consumption.",
    "Men should consume ≤25 g alcohol per day (≈750 mL beer or 250 mL red wine).",
    "Women should consume ≤15 g alcohol per day (≈450 mL beer or 150 mL red wine).",
    "Non-drinkers should not start drinking for 'health benefits'.",
    "If comorbid with diabetes, chronic kidney disease, or coronary heart disease, further individualized adjustments are needed (e.g., stricter salt, protein, or phosphorus control), and medical advice must be followed.",
    "Dietary intervention is highly effective: adherence to low-salt + DASH diet can lower systolic blood pressure by an average of 5–11 mmHg, equivalent to single-drug antihypertensive effect.",
    "For personalized dietary plans (e.g., with comorbid diabetes, kidney disease, or obesity), consultation with a clinical dietitian is recommended."
] 

